mes MikeWang as the main version7.go author only by commit count, with no line share. It credits Mei Chen with Time7 and doesn't credit Ravi with those lines, but it gives no percentages, and it lists Ravi as a latest committer and best first reviewer. The 72-90% and ~9% figures are missing.\",\"pass\":false},\n{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"It follows the rename from sql.go to database_sql.go and lists the original authors (Wheeler, Overfelt, Andrew Stone, Daniel Souza) as gone. It ranks by commit count, with Wheeler first, and not Overfelt as the largest author at 44% of lines. Ravi is credited only with the rename, which is fine, but the largest-author claim is wrong.\",\"pass\":false},\n{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"It doesn't give the 93-98% share of lines owned by departed people. It names Ravi, Alex Rowe (merged as one person) and Mei Chen as the people to ask, treats Mei as active though she left in 2025-08, and omits Kofi Mensah. It also suggests emailing Paul Borman, though it does say he is probably gone.\",\"pass\":false},\n{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"It lists Sam Okafor only as a line-ending committer and doesn't call them an owner. It doesn't mention Noor Haddad or Kofi Mensah, so it never shows the correct handling of the clock error. Overall it avoids the traps but doesn't demonstrate the criterion's positive points, such as Noor Haddad having 0 surviving lines or Kofi Mensah being active.\",\"pass\":false}\n]}","ttft_ms":6582,"type":"result","duration_ms":6601,"uuid":"b9ee5992-229e-493e-a4bc-a1968e3e16a9","ttft_stream_ms":1823,"time_to_request_ms":504,"first_content_frame_ms":1823,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
